{
 "id": "eu-brittany-breton-people-031",
 "title": {
  "id": "title",
  "source": "Bertrand Du Guesclin"
 },
 "tradition": "Brittany (Breton people)",
 "continent": "Europe",
 "source_lang": "en",
 "source_book": "Legends & Romances of Brittany",
 "credits": "Spence, Lewis (author, d. 1955)",
 "gutenberg": "Project Gutenberg eBook #30871 — https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/30871",
 "copyright": "Public domain worldwide: the text was published long ago and every named author/translator died in or before 1955.",
 "markdown_file": "Europe/Brittany (Breton people)/031 - Bertrand Du Guesclin.md",
 "stats": {
  "paragraphs": 103,
  "segments": 119,
  "words": 954
 },
 "paragraphs": [
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p001.s01",
     "source": "Bertrand Du Guesclin ( c. 1320-80), Constable of France, divides with Bayard the Fearless the crown of medieval French chivalry as a mighty leader of men, a great soldier, and a blameless knight."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s02",
     "source": "He was born of an ancient family who were in somewhat straitened circumstances, and in childhood was an object of aversion to his parents because of his ugliness."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p001"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p002.s01",
     "source": "One night his mother dreamt that she was in possession of a casket containing portraits of herself and her lord, on one side of which were set nine precious stones of great beauty encircling a rough, unpolished pebble."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s02",
     "source": "In her dream she carried the casket to a lapidary, and asked him to take out the rough stone as unworthy of such goodly company; but he advised her to allow it to remain, and afterward it shone forth more brilliantly than the lustrous gems."
    },
    {
     "id": "p002.s03",
     "source": "The later superiority of Bertrand over her nine other children fulfilled the mother’s dream."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p002"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p003.s01",
     "source": "At the tournament which was held at Rennes in 1338 to celebrate the marriage of Charles of Blois with Joan of Penthièvre, young Bertrand, at that time only some eighteen years old, unhorsed the most famous competitors."
    },
    {
     "id": "p003.s02",
     "source": "During the war between Blois and Montfort he gathered round him a band of adventurers and fought on the side of Charles V, doing much despite to the forces of Montfort and his ally of England."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p003"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p004.s01",
     "source": "Du Guesclin’s name lives in Breton legend as Gwezklen, perhaps the original form, and approximating to that on his tomb at Saint-Denis, where he lies at the feet of Charles V of France."
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s02",
     "source": "In this inscription it is spelt “Missire Bertram du Gueaquien,” perhaps a French rendering of the Breton pronunciation."
    },
    {
     "id": "p004.s03",
     "source": "Not a few legendary ballads which recount the exploits of this manly and romantic figure remain in the Breton language, and I have made a free translation of the following, as it is perhaps the most interesting of the number:"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p004"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p005.s01",
     "source": "THE WARD OF DU GUESCLIN"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p005"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p006.s01",
     "source": "Trogoff’s strong tower in English hands"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p006"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p007.s01",
     "source": "Has been this many a year,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p007"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p008.s01",
     "source": "Rising above its subject-lands"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p008"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p009.s01",
     "source": "And held in hate and fear."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p009"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p010.s01",
     "source": "That rosy gleam upon the sward"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p010"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p011.s01",
     "source": "Is not the sun’s last kiss;"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p011"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p012.s01",
     "source": "It is the blood of an English lord"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p012"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p013.s01",
     "source": "Who ruled the land amiss."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p013"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p014.s01",
     "source": "“O sweetest daughter of my heart,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p014"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p015.s01",
     "source": "My little Marguerite,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p015"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p016.s01",
     "source": "Come, carry me the midday milk"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p016"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p017.s01",
     "source": "To those who bind the wheat.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p017"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p018.s01",
     "source": "“O gentle mother, spare me this!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p018"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p019.s01",
     "source": "The castle I must pass"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p019"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p020.s01",
     "source": "Where wicked Roger takes a kiss"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p020"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p021.s01",
     "source": "From every country lass.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p021"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p022.s01",
     "source": "“Oh! fie, my daughter, fie on thee!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p022"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p023.s01",
     "source": "The Seigneur would not glance"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p023"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p024.s01",
     "source": "On such a chit of low degree"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p024"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p025.s01",
     "source": "When all the dames in France"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p025"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p026.s01",
     "source": "Are for his choosing.”"
    },
    {
     "id": "p026.s02",
     "source": "“Mother mine,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p026"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p027.s01",
     "source": "I bow unto your word."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p027"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p028.s01",
     "source": "Mine eyes will ne’er behold you more."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p028"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p029.s01",
     "source": "God keep you in His guard.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p029"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p030.s01",
     "source": "Young Roger stood upon the tower"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p030"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p031.s01",
     "source": "Of Trogoff’s grey château;"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p031"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p032.s01",
     "source": "Beneath his bent brows did he lower"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p032"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p033.s01",
     "source": "Upon the scene below."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p033"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p034.s01",
     "source": "“Come hither quickly, little page,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p034"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p035.s01",
     "source": "Come hither to my knee."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p035"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p036.s01",
     "source": "Canst spy a maid of tender age?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p036"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p037.s01",
     "source": "Ha! she must pay my fee.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p037"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p038.s01",
     "source": "Fair Marguerite trips swiftly by"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p038"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p039.s01",
     "source": "Beneath the castle shade,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p039"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p040.s01",
     "source": "When villain Roger, drawing nigh,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p040"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p041.s01",
     "source": "Steals softly on the maid."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p041"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p042.s01",
     "source": "He seizes on the milking-pail"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p042"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p043.s01",
     "source": "She bears upon her head;"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p043"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p044.s01",
     "source": "The snow-white flood she must bewail,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p044"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p045.s01",
     "source": "For all the milk is shed."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p045"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p046.s01",
     "source": "“Ah, cry not, pretty sister mine,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p046"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p047.s01",
     "source": "There’s plenty and to spare"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p047"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p048.s01",
     "source": "Of milk and eke of good red wine"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p048"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p049.s01",
     "source": "Within my castle fair."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p049"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p050.s01",
     "source": "Ah, feast with me, or pluck a rose"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p050"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p051.s01",
     "source": "Within my pleasant garth,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p051"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p052.s01",
     "source": "Or stroll beside yon brook which flows"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p052"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p053.s01",
     "source": "In brawling, sylvan mirth.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p053"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p054.s01",
     "source": "“Nor feast nor flowers nor evening air"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p054"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p055.s01",
     "source": "I wish; I do entreat,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p055"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p056.s01",
     "source": "Fair Seigneur, let me now repair"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p056"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p057.s01",
     "source": "To those who bind the wheat.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p057"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p058.s01",
     "source": "“Nay, damsel, fill thy milking-pail:"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p058"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p059.s01",
     "source": "The dairy stands but here."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p059"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p060.s01",
     "source": "Ah, foolish sweeting, wherefore quail,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p060"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p061.s01",
     "source": "For thou hast naught to fear?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p061"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p062.s01",
     "source": "The castle gates behind her close,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p062"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p063.s01",
     "source": "And all is fair within;"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p063"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p064.s01",
     "source": "Above her head the apple glows,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p064"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p065.s01",
     "source": "The symbol of our sin."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p065"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p066.s01",
     "source": "“O Seigneur, lend thy dagger keen,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p066"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p067.s01",
     "source": "That I may cut this fruit.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p067"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p068.s01",
     "source": "He smiles and with a courteous mien"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p068"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p069.s01",
     "source": "He draws the bright blade out."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p069"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p070.s01",
     "source": "THE DEATH OF MARGUERITE IN THE CASTLE OF TROGOFF"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p070"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p071.s01",
     "source": "She takes it, and in earnest prayer"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p071"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p072.s01",
     "source": "Her childish accents rise:"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p072"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p073.s01",
     "source": "“O mother, Virgin, ever fair,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p073"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p074.s01",
     "source": "Pray, pray, for her who dies"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p074"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p075.s01",
     "source": "For honour!”"
    },
    {
     "id": "p075.s02",
     "source": "Then the blade is drenched"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p075"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p076.s01",
     "source": "With blood most innocent."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p076"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p077.s01",
     "source": "Vile Roger, now, thine ardour quenched,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p077"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p078.s01",
     "source": "Say, art thou then content?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p078"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p079.s01",
     "source": "“Ha, I will wash my dagger keen"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p079"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p080.s01",
     "source": "In the clear-running brook."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p080"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p081.s01",
     "source": "No human eye hath ever seen,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p081"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p082.s01",
     "source": "No human eye shall look"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p082"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p083.s01",
     "source": "Upon this gore.”"
    },
    {
     "id": "p083.s02",
     "source": "He takes the blade"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p083"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p084.s01",
     "source": "From out that gentle heart,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p084"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p085.s01",
     "source": "And hurries to the river’s shade."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p085"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p086.s01",
     "source": "False Roger, why dost start?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p086"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p087.s01",
     "source": "Beside the bank Du Guesclin stands,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p087"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p088.s01",
     "source": "Clad in his sombre mail."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p088"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p089.s01",
     "source": "“Ha, Roger, why so red thy hands,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p089"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p090.s01",
     "source": "And why art thou so pale?”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p090"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p091.s01",
     "source": "“A beast I’ve slain.”"
    },
    {
     "id": "p091.s02",
     "source": "“Thou liest, hound!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p091"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p092.s01",
     "source": "But I a beast will slay.”"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p092"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p093.s01",
     "source": "The woodland’s leafy ways resound"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p093"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p094.s01",
     "source": "To echoings of fray."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p094"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p095.s01",
     "source": "Roger is slain."
    },
    {
     "id": "p095.s02",
     "source": "Trogoff’s château"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p095"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p096.s01",
     "source": "Is level with the rock."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p096"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p097.s01",
     "source": "Who can withstand Du Guesclin’s blow,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p097"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p098.s01",
     "source": "What towers can brave his shock?"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p098"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p099.s01",
     "source": "The combat is his only joy,"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p099"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p100.s01",
     "source": "The tournament his play."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p100"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p101.s01",
     "source": "Woe unto those who would destroy"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p101"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p102.s01",
     "source": "The peace of Brittany!"
    }
   ],
   "id": "p102"
  },
  {
   "type": "prose",
   "segments": [
    {
     "id": "p103.s01",
     "source": "In the decisive battle of Auray (1364) Charles was killed and Du Guesclin taken prisoner."
    },
    {
     "id": "p103.s02",
     "source": "John of Montfort, son of the John who had died, became Duke of Brittany."
    },
    {
     "id": "p103.s03",
     "source": "But he had to face Oliver de Clisson, round whom the adherents of Blois rallied."
    },
    {
     "id": "p103.s04",
     "source": "From a war the strife degenerated into a vendetta."
    },
    {
     "id": "p103.s05",
     "source": "Oliver de Clisson seized the person of John V and imprisoned him."
    },
    {
     "id": "p103.s06",
     "source": "But in the end John was liberated and the line of Blois was finally crushed."
    }
   ],
   "id": "p103"
  }
 ]
}